WEBVTT

00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:01.769
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:07.130
In this lesson, we will represent apparatus, crews, and gps devices.

00:00:07.619 --> 00:00:11.399
A vehicle name alone does not tell a dispatcher its type, home

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:14.060
station, crew, or location source.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.639
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:19.579
practical way to check the result.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.849
Engine 1 and Rescue 1 are added with their unit types and assigned to Station 1.

00:00:25.419 --> 00:00:28.940
Units let dispatchers send the right resources and let everyone

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.829
see which apparatus is available.

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:34.789
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:34.789 --> 00:00:37.050
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.329
Units.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:41.650
Your apparatus, vehicles and response teams.

00:00:42.189 --> 00:00:45.279
Add each unit with its type and home station group.

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:46.760
Unit types.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:50.460
Categories such as Engine, Ladder or Ambulance.

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:55.099
Create unit types before adding units so each unit can be classified.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.500
Hardware location tracking.

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:00.749
GPS devices that report unit locations.

00:01:01.169 --> 00:01:04.359
Register each tracking device and link it to its unit.

00:01:04.919 --> 00:01:05.700
New Unit.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.550
Add an apparatus, vehicle or team.

00:01:09.029 --> 00:01:13.089
List your apparatus or response teams with their types and home stations.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:17.910
Teams that respond only as individuals can mark this module not applicable.

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:19.510
Unit Staffing.

00:01:19.919 --> 00:01:21.750
Assign crew members to units.

00:01:22.139 --> 00:01:26.230
List your apparatus or response teams with their types and home stations.

00:01:26.569 --> 00:01:31.029
Teams that respond only as individuals can mark this module not applicable.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.459
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:01:34.959 --> 00:01:35.560
Step 1.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.340
Create Engine and Rescue unit types.

00:01:38.749 --> 00:01:39.439
Step 2.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.869
Add Engine 1 with its type, Station 1, and crew roles.

00:01:44.239 --> 00:01:45.010
Step 3.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.130
Assign the crew and, when used, register a tracking device against the unit.

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:52.309
Now verify the result.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.640
Confirm the unit type, home station, crew, and status.

00:01:56.959 --> 00:02:00.310
For hardware tracking, check a recent received position and

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:01.810
the stale-position behavior.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:07.300
A common problem to watch for: An old GPS position is not a live position.

00:02:07.709 --> 00:02:12.070
Crew assignment, reported unit status, and physical readiness are distinct.

00:02:12.669 --> 00:02:14.210
Your practice task is simple.

00:02:14.689 --> 00:02:18.289
Create Engine 1 in the demo department and verify the assigned

00:02:18.289 --> 00:02:19.720
crew from the dispatcher view.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:22.250
Measure incomplete unit records.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:26.450
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

